# Normalize line endings for every text file in this repository.
#
# The committed blobs are already LF (verified: the index contains no CRLF),
# but Windows checkouts have core.autocrlf=true and there was no .gitattributes,
# so git rewrote a subset of files to CRLF on checkout. That made "gofmt -l"
# report four Go files as unformatted on Windows even though CI (Linux, LF)
# passed - a false positive that hides real formatting drift.
#
# Force LF in the working tree on every platform so local tooling matches CI.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must be LF or they fail to run under bash.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Windows-only helper scripts, if ever added, keep CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary assets are never normalized.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary
*.tar binary
